    "result_text": "Tests are green. \n\n## What I changed\n\nI agreed with the finding \u2014 the per-city count expression was duplicated across `CheckOwnerCityCapacity` and `AssignOwnerCustomerCode`, and both encode the same \"owners in a city\" domain primitive meant to stay consistent.\n\nFollowing the existing `OwnerHousehold`/`OwnerAddress` precedent (package-private `final` helper, single source of truth), I:\n\n1. **Added `OwnerCity.java`** with `countOwnersInCity(OwnerRepository, String city)` \u2014 the one place the \"same city\" definition now lives, with a Javadoc noting that case-insensitive alignment would be a one-place change.\n2. **Updated `CheckOwnerCityCapacity`** to call the helper (and dropped its now-unused `Owner` import).\n3. **Updated `AssignOwnerCustomerCode`** to call the same helper for its per-city sequence.\n\nBehaviour is unchanged (exact city matching, `\u2265 50 \u2192 409`); the full suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
